/-!
# Lifting the perfect FF alternatives

Basic proves the star-component models and their orbit bounds for an actual
quasisimple actor or a product of two quasisimple actors. A noncentral cubic
witness in each model gives the universal equality L = [L,Y₀] using the local
normalizer and theta identities and solvability of Y₀. The latter solvability
is derived from the earlier extraspecial alternative, without assuming that
M ∩ H is solvable.

Models fixes the concrete group catalogue for these branches. Its constructors
carry actual equivalences; they assert neither classification nor model facts.
The natural, double-natural, indecomposable, and hyperplane module alternatives
do not change Basic's group-theoretic commutator argument.

Final source assembly remains unfinished. Basic only proves that the
C-component layer is the solvable residual and that J = J∞ (J ∩ O₂(H)).
Absorption of J ∩ O₂(H) must still be derived from the genuine earlier local
hypotheses and the provenance A = Vα. The noncentral cubic witnesses must also
be constructed for Models. No component-generation or strong-offender
conclusion is assumed, and this module does not yet assert 15.3.49(i).

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), B.5.6,
printed pp.99–110, and the proof of 15.3.49(i), printed pp.1143–1144.
-/
